{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_a3e524527915",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 582,
      "mechanism": "Replaces combinational assignment `o_wb_ack <= wb_stb` with registered pipeline `q_wb_ack <= wb_stb; o_wb_ack <= q_wb_ack`. This adds one cycle latency to the Wishbone acknowledge, directly addressing the observed early/late `o_wb_ack` toggles at cycles 6, 7, 11, 12, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 25 in the public trace."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_26769e648dd1",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 8371,
      "mechanism": "Guards the full command-dispatch reset block with `!pre_cmd_state`. In the original, `!ll_cmd_stb` alone triggers state clear on every cycle while the low-level transmitter is idle; with the pipeline acknowledge (patch_a3e524527915) the design now has an extra cycle where `ll_cmd_stb` is already low but the new command has not yet been sampled, so the extra guard prevents premature clearing of `r_cmd_state`, `r_use_fifo`, `r_data_fil`, etc. that would corrupt the next command/response sequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6083bec9b350",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9734,
      "mechanism": "Changes the R1-without-FIFO branch from `SDSPI_RSP_WRITING` to `SDSPI_RSP_NONE`. The trace shows the design must not enter a FIFO-write response state when no FIFO is configured; the original unqualified assignment forces `second_rsp_state` into WRITING, which later drives `ll_fifo_wr` and watchdog logic, perturbing `o_wb_ack` timing."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_afa0971cd501",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9603,
      "mechanism": "Qualifies the transition into `r_cmd_state == 3'h4` (CRC byte transmission) with `r_have_resp`. Without this, the state machine advances to CRC transmit before the SD card response token has been seen, causing `ll_cmd_stb` to stay asserted too long and shifting the acknowledge pipeline."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_574faa6d7168",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9969,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `(r_use_fifo)&&(r_fifo_wr)` with `((r_use_fifo)&&(r_fifo_wr)) && (ll_fifo_rd_complete)` when deciding whether to issue a dummy 0xFE byte during FIFO read. This prevents the transmitter from sending extra bytes before the low-level RX path has signaled `ll_fifo_rd_complete`, which would otherwise hold `ll_cmd_stb` high and delay `o_wb_ack` de-assertion."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e69de1c27f07",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9969,
      "mechanism": "Adds `!ll_fifo_rd_complete` guard to the same condition as patch_574faa6d7168 but for the write-direction token (0xFE emission during FIFO write). Prevents premature token emission that would keep `ll_cmd_stb` asserted and misalign the acknowledge pipeline."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_8cf8e76d1134",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9810,
      "mechanism": "Changes the `r_use_fifo` register load enable from bare `r_use_fifo` to `(r_use_fifo) && (r_have_resp)`. This ensures the FIFO-direction bit is only updated after the first response token arrives, avoiding a stale `r_use_fifo` value that would misroute the command state machine and perturb acknowledge timing."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_436fc440e456",
      "failure_port": "o_wb_ack",
      "source_line": 9603,
      "mechanism": "Guards the `r_cmd_state == 3'h4` (CRC byte) transition with `!r_have_resp`. This is the complement of patch_afa0971cd501: it prevents the state machine from *skipping* the CRC byte when a response *has* already arrived, keeping the byte-level transmit sequence cycle-exact with the SD card protocol."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The public trace shows ten `o_wb_ack` mismatches in the first 25 cycles, all of which are single-cycle early/late toggles. This pattern is characteristic of a missing pipeline register on the acknowledge path. patch_a3e524527915 adds that register and is therefore the primary fix. The remaining seven patches are condition gates that prevent the command/response state machine from taking incorrect transitions while the new acknowledge pipeline changes the relative timing of `ll_cmd_stb`, `r_cmd_busy`, and `pre_cmd_state`. Each gate addresses a specific transition (CRC byte, FIFO token emission, response-state selection, FIFO-direction capture) that would otherwise drift by one cycle and re-introduce acknowledge errors. Together the eight patches form a minimal, cycle-exact correction set for the observed trace."
}
